  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: httpclient5 5.6.0.rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5 5.6.0.rhlw-00001 with a backported security fix.\n\nCVE-2026-40542: Missing critical step in authentication in Apache HttpClient 5.6 allows an attacker to cause the client to accept SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication without proper mutual authentication verification. Users are recommended to upgrade to version 5.6.1, which fixes this issue.\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.httpcomponents.client5:httpclient5 5.6.0 from Maven Central.",
